      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Krea 2 inpainting\n\nRepaints the masked area of an image with Krea 2 Turbo (a regular, non-inpaint model; Krea ships no inpaint checkpoint)\nthe way Forge's \"Inpaint upload\" does. **Inpaint Crop** cuts the masked area with some context out of the image and\nscales it to the generation size, so that even a small area is sampled at full resolution; **Inpaint Stitch** scales\nthe result back and blends it into the original through the blurred mask. **Differential Diffusion** makes the soft\nmask edge blend gradually.\n\n**Settings**: 8 steps, CFG 1, euler, simple, denoising 0.9. The negative conditioning is zeroed (CFG 1). For more\ncontrol use Raw (`krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors`): about 52 steps, CFG 3.5, with a negative prompt node marked `ib:np`.\n\nRequires [ComfyUI-Inpaint-CropAndStitch](https://github.com/lquesada/ComfyUI-Inpaint-CropAndStitch) (install it with\nthe ComfyUI Manager).\n\n## Image Bench\n\nThe Generate tab is in **Inpaint** mode while this workflow is loaded.\n\n| Marker / node | Generate tab |\n|---------------|--------------|\n| `ib:img` Load Image | Input cell; \"Send image\" from the editor |\n| `ib:mask` Load Image Mask | Mask cell; the editor selection |\n| `ib:cp`, `ib:pp` | model, prompt and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` KSampler | seed, steps, CFG scale, sampling method, schedule type, denoising |\n| Inpaint Crop | Resize to (`output_target_width/height`), Mask blur (`mask_blend_pixels`), Mask mode (`mask_invert`) |\n| Only masked padding (Grow Mask) | Only masked padding, pixels |\n| Whole picture (Solid Mask) | Inpaint area: value 0 = Only masked, 1 = Whole picture |\n\nThe loaders refer to the files the editor plugins write (`image_bench_photoshop_*.png`); send an image and a mask, or\nset them in the Input / Mask cells of the Generate tab, before the first queue.\n\n- **Only masked**: the model sees only the crop (the mask's bounding box plus the padding, widened to the aspect\n  ratio of the size). Describe what the crop shows, the new content of the masked area and its surroundings, in\n  full sentences.\n- **Whole picture**: the whole image is scaled to the size and sampled; describe the whole image.\n- Denoising 0.85-1.0 replaces the content, 0.4-0.7 keeps its colors and shapes; at 8 steps a low denoising leaves\n  only a few steps, so raise the steps for subtle changes.\n- Mask blur widens the mask by that many pixels and blurs it; the pixels outside the mask within that distance are\n  blended too.\n- Krea 2 works up to 2048×2048; keep the crop size near 1-2 MP.\n\n## Model Links\n\n[Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2) also has `*_bf16` and `*_int8_convrot` diffusion models of\nRaw and Turbo, `krea2_turbo_mxfp8` / `krea2_turbo_nvfp4` (RTX 50), and the bf16 / int8 text encoders.\n\n**diffusion_models**: [krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors), [krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors)\n**text_encoders**: [qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors) (one file for Raw and Turbo)\n**vae**: [qwen_image_vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_vae.safetensors) (the Qwen-Image VAE)\n\nKrea 2 is released under the Krea 2 Community License.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: Krea 2 inpainting",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
